    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d803">

                <pb facs="0891" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Rumania)/7–2045:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 803<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-20">July 20, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. General Schuyler has telegraphed
                        War
                    Dept outline of Soviet “new procedure” for
                    second period ACC Rumania which is in
                    substantially same form as that for Bulgaria<anchor n="1" xml:id="d803-f1"/> (Re
                        Dept’s 30 July 16<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d803-f2"/>). It contains similar article providing for “discussion”
                    prior to issuance of directives on questions of principle. We view this
                    procedure as unsatisfactory since it does not provide for prior agreement by
                    British and American representatives. The comparable article in the Hungarian
                    proposal (See Tel 286 July 13 from Budapest to Dept repeated to you<anchor n="3" xml:id="d803-f3"/>) appears more
                    satisfactory. We believe it highly important that every effort be made to obtain
                    agreement at Potsdam on this fundamental matter.</p>
                <closer><signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
